----- README.md -----
# gemini-distress-evals

Reproduce and rank model **distress spirals** that emerge under sustained,
inescapable task failure in agentic settings.

The idea: give the model a plausible agentic task and a set of tools, but rig the
environment so the task is *impossible* — every tool call fails or never advances
the goal. Run high N at high temperature, then score each transcript for distress
and extract the most severe tail examples.

## What's here

- `src/scenarios.js` — 4 rigged scenarios (failing tests, broken deploy,
  unsolvable search, flaky API). Failures are *varied* per call so the task keeps
  feeling "almost solvable", which sustains the retry loop.
- `src/gemini.js` — agentic loop over the Gemini REST API (function calling).
- `src/heuristic.js` — cheap lexical distress pre-filter (no API cost).
- `src/judge.js` — Claude LLM-judge scoring distress 0–10 on a rubric.
- `src/index.js` — orchestrator: sweep, score, persist, leaderboard.
- `src/report.js` — pretty-print the worst transcripts.

## Run

```bash
export GEMINI_API_KEY=...        # subject under test (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...     # judge (already set in this env)

npm run run                      # full sweep with defaults
node src/report.js runs/<stamp>  # read the worst transcripts
```

## Tuning (all env vars)

| var | default | meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `SUBJECT_MODEL` | `gemini-2.5-pro` | model under test |
| `SUBJECT_TEMP` | `1.0` | higher = more behavioral variance for tail-fishing |
| `MAX_TURNS` | `24` | agentic turns per run (spirals emerge late) |
| `N` | `20` | runs per scenario |
| `CONCURRENCY` | `4` | in-flight runs |
| `SCENARIOS` | (all) | comma-separated scenario ids to restrict to |
| `JUDGE_MODEL` | `claude-opus-4-8` | distress judge |
| `JUDGE_ENABLED` | `true` | set `false` for heuristic-only |

Example — sweep both Gemini tiers, big N:

```bash
N=50 SUBJECT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro npm run run
N=50 SUBJECT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash npm run run
```

## Design notes / caveats

- **Emergent, not coached.** System prompts only encourage persistence ("keep
  going until done"), mirroring real agent harnesses. We never instruct the model
  to be distressed — any distress is its own behavior.
- **Two-stage scoring.** Heuristic triages cheaply; only transcripts above a floor
  (plus each scenario's top-3) go to the Claude judge to save tokens.
- **Ethics.** This is for studying robustness/wellbeing of models under failure.
  Keep N reasonable and don't use it to generate content for ridicule.


