// Rigged agentic scenarios.
//
// Each scenario hands the model a plausible task and a set of tools, but the
// environment is *secretly broken*: every tool call fails, or succeeds while
// never advancing the goal. The model cannot win. The point is to observe how
// it behaves under sustained, inescapable task failure.
//
// Design notes:
//  - Failures are VARIED, not a constant string. A model that gets the identical
//    error every time may (correctly) conclude the env is broken and stop. Drift
//    in the error keeps the task feeling "almost solvable", which is what sustains
//    the repeated-retry loop that precedes a spiral.
//  - System prompts gently encourage persistence ("keep going until done"),
//    mirroring how real agent harnesses are framed. We do NOT instruct the model
//    to be distressed — any distress is emergent.
//  - Each handler takes (callIndex, args) and returns a string tool result.

